Package: python3-skyshutter
Architecture: all
Depends:
 ${misc:Depends},
 ${python3:Depends},
Description: Control a Nikon Coolpix camera over its own WiFi via PTP/IP
 skyshutter speaks PTP/IP to the camera's own access point: pairing
 handshake (BLE), live view, shutter release and property access. The
 core client is pure stdlib; bench tools may pull optional extras.
 .
 This package ships the library and the `skyshutter` CLI.

Package: skyshutter-pi
Architecture: all
Depends:
 python3-skyshutter,
 ${misc:Depends},
Recommends:
 python3-bleak,
 python3-pycryptodome,
Description: Field-rig meta package for skyshutter
 Pulls python3-skyshutter plus the BLE stack used on the Raspberry Pi
 rig and installs the systemd user units (ble-watch, pair-agent) as
 examples under /usr/share/doc/skyshutter-pi/examples/.
